{"name":"Goose Down","hex":"#f4e7df","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"goose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various grazing waterfowl of the family Anatidae, which have feathers and webbed feet and are capable of flying, swimming, and walking on land, and which are generally bigger than ducks.","A female goose."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To sharply poke or pinch the buttocks, or prod between the buttocks (of a person).","To stimulate; to spur."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/goose"},{"term":"down","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["From a higher position to a lower one; downwards.","To or towards what is considered the bottom of something, irrespective of whether this is presently physically lower."]},{"part":"Preposition","definitions":["From the higher end to the lower of.","From north to south of."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/down"}],"entries":[{"title":"Down feather","blocks":[{"text":"The down of birds is a layer of fine feathers found under the tougher exterior feathers. Very young birds are clad only in down. Powder down is a specialized type of down found only in a few groups of birds. Down is a fine thermal insulator and padding, used in goods such as jackets, bedding, pillows and sleeping bags. The discovery of feathers trapped in ancient amber suggests that some species of non-avian dinosaur likely possessed down-like feathers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Donsvlokje.jpg/330px-Donsvlokje.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Down_feather","wikidata":"Q953515"},{"title":"Goose","blocks":[{"text":"A goose is a bird of any of several waterfowl species in the family Anatidae. This group comprises the genera Anser and Branta. Some members of the Tadorninae subfamily are commonly called geese, but are not considered \"true geese\" taxonomically. More distantly related members of the family Anatidae are swans, most of which are larger than true geese, and ducks, which are smaller."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/37/Anser_anser_1_%28Piotr_Kuczynski%29_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Anser_anser_1_%28Piotr_Kuczynski%29_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goose","wikidata":"Q16529344"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Chick.jpg/500px-Chick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Chick.jpg/1280px-Chick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Chick.jpg/500px-Chick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Like many precocial hatchlings, domestic chickens are already covered with a coat of downy feathers when they hatch.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChick.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Bird_Imprint_on_Window_0069.jpg/500px-Bird_Imprint_on_Window_0069.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Bird_Imprint_on_Window_0069.jpg/500px-Bird_Imprint_on_Window_0069.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Feather dust\" left on a window after a birdstrike","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABird_Imprint_on_Window_0069.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Melopsittacus_undulatus_-_male_pet_preening.jpg/500px-Melopsittacus_undulatus_-_male_pet_preening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e